  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Port Orleans French Quarter is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>People who want a smaller Moderate.</strong> This side of Port Orleans is more compact than Riverside, and you are close to the food court, the pool and the boat dock if you book a Preferred room.</li>
      <li><strong>Anyone who wants a boat to Disney Springs.</strong> Official water transportation listings show the Sassagoula River Cruise from French Quarter, Riverside, Old Key West and Saratoga Springs.</li>
      <li><strong>Families of four who want two queen beds</strong> at a Moderate rate. In 2026 a Standard Location room ran about $322 to $483 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed for a child, or a more themed "Royal" room.</strong> Those are on the Riverside side, not here.</li>
      <li><strong>You want several table-service restaurants on site.</strong> The food court is the main option while Scat Cat's Club is under refurbishment. Riverside's Boatwright's Dining Hall is a walk or a short boat ride away.</li>
      <li><strong>Your parks are the main event and you want a Skyliner or monorail.</strong> Theme parks are buses from here.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
